// The refused generic assert_eq spelling: a generic body refuses
// through every door it needs — the abort shape first (the panic
// return's type variable never solves inside the if arm, so the
// arm's value unions it into a `() | t` that does not fit the unit
// answer), the equality compare underneath (the checker admits `==`
// over a type variable and the lowering refuses it — no uop covers a
// variable's runtime word kind, the reflection seam the
// per-instantiation frames own), and the message rendering beside
// them (the interpolation hole's `show` dispatch never solves over a
// variable). The landed members are the concrete per-width spellings.

fn assert_eq_any[t] (a: t, b: t, msg: string) -> () {
  if !(a == b) { panic(msg) }
}

fn main() -> int {
  assert_eq_any(1, 1, "ints")
  0
}
